description:
calendars-client/src/methods/principal_availability.rs:70 has a test `empty_principal_id_returns_invalid_argument` that does NOT exercise the actual code path:

```rust
let result: Result<(), _> = if "".is_empty() {
    Err(ClientError::InvalidArgument("must not be empty".into()))
} else {
    Ok(())
};
assert!(matches!(result, Err(ClientError::InvalidArgument(_))));
```

The `if "".is_empty()` is always true (clippy::const_is_empty caught this and was muted with #[allow]). The test never calls into get_availability or whatever the actual method is named. It just constructs ClientError::InvalidArgument and asserts the constructed value matches the variant — vacuous.

Per AGENTS.md: 'Never write a test that uses the code under test as its own oracle. Tests must have an independent oracle.' This test fails the principle — it has no real oracle.

Same vacuous pattern likely exists in task_notification (the subagent reported the test 'mirrors' that crate). Audit and fix all instances together.

Fix options:
1. Delete the vacuous tests entirely.
2. Rewrite to actually call principal_availability with an empty principal_id and verify the error.

The pre-existing #[allow(clippy::const_is_empty)] should be removed once the test is rewritten.
